    48	## 1. Setting
    49	
    50	- X ≥ 1 is an integer and the box is 𝔅₀ = (0, X]² ∩ Z².
    51	- The band 𝒫 is a nonempty set of primes in (Y, 2Y].
    52	- V is a nonempty set of coprime (A,B) ∈ [1,H]². D′ uses V(H), which also requires A ≠ B;
    53	  that is not needed here.
    54	- s = Σ_{ℓ∈𝒫} 1/ℓ and λ = |V|·s. |𝒫| is the number of band primes.
    55	- For x = (a,b) and v = (A,B), write F_v(x) = Ba − Ab = det(x, v).
    56	  - z_ℓ(x) = #{v ∈ V : ℓ | F_v(x)}.
    57	  - W(x) = #{ℓ ∈ 𝒫 : z_ℓ(x) > 0}.
    58	  - x is *uncovered* iff W(x) = 0. For a prime pair this is exactly D′'s condition
    59	    "no (v,ℓ) with ℓ | Bp − Aq".
    60	- ℒ = ∪_{v∈V} R·v is the union of the lines through the weights, and 𝔅 = 𝔅₀ ∖ ℒ.
    61	  - Points of ℒ are covered by every band prime.
    62	  - No prime pair p ≠ q, with p, q > H, lies on ℒ: Bp = Aq forces p | A ≤ H.
    63	- A *configuration* of order j is c = ((ℓ₁,v₁), …, (ℓ_j,v_j)) with **distinct** ℓ_i ∈ 𝒫
    64	  and v_i ∈ V. Its lattice is Λ_c = {x ∈ Z² : ℓ_i | F_{v_i}(x) ∀i}, and d_c = ∏ℓ_i.
    65	- The model: Z = Σ_ℓ Z_ℓ with independent Z_ℓ ~ Bernoulli(|V|/ℓ). Then
    66	  E(Z)_j = Σ_c 1/d_c, where (w)_j = w(w−1)⋯(w−j+1).
