   130	  Then d ≥ (√3/2)|b₁||b₂|.
   131	- In coordinates x = σb₁ + τb₂, Λ becomes Z². K becomes a convex set K′ of area area(K)/d.
   132	- σ(x) = det(x,b₂)/det(b₁,b₂) varies over K by at most D|b₂|/d ≤ (2/√3)D/ρ. Likewise τ
   133	  varies by at most D|b₁|/d ≤ (2/√3)D/ρ.
   134	- Count Z² ∩ K′ column by column.
   135	  - Each column σ ∈ Z meets K′ in an interval of length h(σ), containing between h(σ) − 1
   136	    and h(σ) + 1 integers.
   137	  - There are at most w_σ + 1 nonempty columns, where w_σ is the width of K′ in σ.
   138	  - h is concave on its support, hence unimodal. So |Σ_σ h(σ) − area(K′)| ≤ max h ≤ w_τ.
   139	- Hence |# − area(K′)| ≤ w_σ + w_τ + 1. ∎
