   186	    - Each nonempty line carries h(mg)/|u| ± 1 lattice points, and there are at most
   187	      2HX/g values m ≠ 0 with |mg| < HX.
   188	    - Dropping m = 0 (the removed line Rv) costs ≤ h(0)/|u|.
   189	    - Since g|u| = d|v|, we get |#(Λ_c ∩ 𝔅₀ ∖ Rv) − X²/d| ≤ (max h + h(0))/|u| + 2HX/g.
   190	  - Subtracting the other ℒ-lines as in (a) completes the proof. ∎
   191	
   192	### 2.4 Summation over configurations — proved
   193	
   194	Let Σ_c run over the configurations of order j. Then
   195	
   196	  Σ_c |#(Λ_c ∩ 𝔅) − X²/d_c| ≤ A_j + B_j + C_j + D_j + E_j.
   197	
   198	- **A_j:** the "+1" of case (i), summed over at most (|𝒫||V|)^j configurations.
   199	- **B_j:** in case (i), c is counted at its own shortest vector u = u_c ∉ ℒ, with
   200	  |u| ≤ R_j := 1.0746(2Y)^{j/2}.
   201	  - For such u, each F_v(u) is nonzero with |F_v(u)| ≤ √2H·R_j ≤ 6.1HY² < Y³ (Y > 6.1H).
   202	    So F_v(u) has ≤ 2 band prime factors.
   203	  - Hence u satisfies ≤ 2|V| events (ℓ, v), and lies in Λ_c for ≤ (2|V|)^j configurations.
   204	  - With Σ_{0<|u|≤R} 1/|u| ≤ 8R (there are 8m vectors with |u|_∞ = m, each with |u| ≥ m):
   205	    Σ_{case (i)} 3.266X/|u_c| ≤ 3.266X·8R_j(2|V|)^j ≤ B_j.
   206	- **C_j:** swap the sum over c with the sum over v′.
   207	  - For fixed v′ and r, Σ_{c: r_{v′}(c)=r} 1/t_{v′}(c) ≤ C(j,r)·λ^r·|𝒫|^{j−r}. Choose the r
   208	    positions; each of them contributes Σ_{ℓ,v} 1/ℓ = λ, and each other position contributes
   209	    a factor ≤ |𝒫|. Dropping distinctness only enlarges the sum.
   210	  - Σ_{v′} 1/max(A′,B′) ≤ Σ_{m≤H}(2m−1)/m < 2H.
   211	- **D_j:** case (ii) with j − r ≥ 4 occurs only for j = 4 and r = 0 (all four labels equal).
   212	  The error is X²/d, and Σ_v Σ X²/(ℓ₁⋯ℓ₄) ≤ |V|X²s⁴.
   213	- **E_j:** case (ii) with j − r ≤ 3, so r ∈ I_j.
   214	  - Σ_{c: r_v=r} 1/t_v ≤ C(j,r)λ^r|𝒫|^{j−r} and Σ_{c: r_v=r} 1/g ≤ C(j,r)s^{j−r}(|𝒫||V|)^r.
   215	  - Σ_v 2√2X/|v| ≤ 2√2X·2H ≤ 6HX.
   216	
   217	### 2.5 Factorial moments and assembly — proved
   218	
   219	- Put F_j(x) := Σ_c 1[x ∈ Λ_c] = Σ_{ℓ₁,…,ℓ_j distinct} ∏ z_{ℓ_i}(x).
   220	  - By (F1), F_j(x) = (W(x))_j unless x ∈ 𝒟 := {x : ∃ℓ ∈ 𝒫, ℓ | a, ℓ | b}.
   221	  - On 𝔅 both lie in [0, (Σ_ℓ z_ℓ)^j] ⊂ [0, (3|V|)^j] by (F2).
   222	  - #(𝒟 ∩ 𝔅₀) ≤ X²Σ_ℓ ℓ^{−2} ≤ X²s/Y.
   223	  - Hence |Σ_{𝔅}(W)_j − Σ_c #(Λ_c∩𝔅)| ≤ F_j (the table entry), and
   224	    |Σ_𝔅 (W)_j − X²E(Z)_j| ≤ Err_j.
   225	- For j = 0: |#𝔅 − X²| = #(ℒ ∩ 𝔅₀) ≤ Σ_v X/max(A,B) < 2HX.
   226	- Expand in falling factorials, using Stirling numbers:
   227	  (w−λ)⁴ = (w)₄ + (6−4λ)(w)₃ + (7−12λ+6λ²)(w)₂ + (1−4λ+6λ²−4λ³)(w)₁ + λ⁴.
   228	  - For λ ≥ 1 the coefficients are bounded by κ_j.
   229	  - The same identity holds for Z, and E(Z−λ)⁴ = Σ_ℓ μ₄(Z_ℓ) + 3Σ_{ℓ≠ℓ′}σ_ℓ²σ_ℓ′² ≤ λ + 3λ².
   230	    A Bernoulli(π) variable has μ₄ = π(1−π)(1−3π+3π²) ≤ π and σ² ≤ π.
   231	- Every uncovered x ∈ 𝔅 contributes (0−λ)⁴ = λ⁴. So
   232	
   233	  λ⁴·#{W=0} ≤ Σ_𝔅 (W−λ)⁴ ≤ X²(3λ²+λ) + λ⁴·2HX + Σ_{j=1}^{4} κ_j Err_j. ∎
   234	
   235	**Remarks.**
   236	- (1) The repeated-direction (same-slope) degeneracy is essential. Exact equidistribution is
   237	  false for 4 equal labels: the count is 0, not X²/d (case (ii), j − r ≥ 4). Removing ℒ, as
   238	  the orchestrator/r16 warned, is what makes it harmless (row D).
   239	- (2) The weight-free statistic Q = mean of (1 − M/λ)⁴ of the pre-registration (P5) is this
   240	  fourth moment.
