   484	### 5.3 Why P5 failed (post hoc, exploratory X1; not pre-registered)
   485	
   486	- In the integer model, x ≡ (0,0) (mod ℓ) has probability 1/ℓ² and gives M_ℓ = |V|.
   487	- With 10⁶ samples the number of such points is O(1)–O(10) per cell. Yet the model's fourth
   488	  moment contains |V|⁴Σ_ℓ ℓ^{−2}, which is dominated by them. So the sample m4 is a
   489	  heavy-tailed Poisson draw: mostly far below the model, occasionally above.
   490	- This is the set 𝒟 of §2.5. The proof also treats it separately and bounds it crudely (row F).
