   283	**Proposition 4 (one-variable large sieve with a prime presieve; proved, standard).**
   284	|E_b|/|S_n| ≤ C/(1 + λ_min) = O(n/H²).
   285	
   286	*Proof.*
   287	- Fix a prime q and a block k. Let U(q) be the set of *prime* p ∈ (P/2, P] uncovered by block k.
   288	- Put Q = ⌊√P⌋ and Z = ⌊Q/2^{k+1}Y⌋. Then 1 ≤ Z < Y and ln Z ≥ (1/6 − o(1))·ln P.
   289	- U(q) avoids the |V| classes AqB^{−1} mod each ℓ ∈ 𝒫_k, and the class 0 mod each prime r ≤ Z,
   290	  since p > P/2 > Z.
   291	- The arithmetic large sieve (Montgomery 1968; Montgomery–Vaughan 1973) gives
   292	  |U(q)| ≤ (P/2 + 1 + Q²)/J.
   293	- In J, keep d = m and d = mℓ, with m ≤ Z squarefree and ℓ ∈ 𝒫_k.
   294	  - These d are ≤ Q and pairwise distinct, because the primes of m are < Y < ℓ.
   295	  - So J ≥ (Σ_{m≤Z} μ²(m)/φ(m))·(1 + Σ_ℓ |V|/(ℓ−|V|)) ≥ (1+λ_k)·ln Z.
   296	- Summing over the ≤ 3P/n primes q gives |E_b| ≤ C P²/(n²(1+λ)). ∎
   297	
   298	This is the r16 / sieve2d_1 refinement. I verified it line by line. It removes D′'s n-loss but
   299	not the power of λ.
