   301	**Theorem 3 (cost/exception trade-off; proved).** Let ε′ ∈ (0, 1/80] and n ≥ n₀(ε′). The
   302	algorithm DCL-det_{n,ε′} of D′ §2, unchanged, has:
   303	- H = ⌈n·2^{ε′n/2}⌉;
   304	- cost N^{1/6+5ε′/6}(log N)^{O(1)};
   305	- at most C·2^{−2ε′n}·|S_n| FAIL pairs.
   306	
   307	Restated with ε = 2ε′: **N^{−ε} exceptions at cost N^{1/6+5ε/12}(log N)^{O(1)}, for
   308	ε ≤ 1/40.** Equivalently, cost N^{1/6+δ+o(1)} with an exceptional fraction O(N^{−12δ/5}),
   309	for δ ≤ 1/96.
   310	
   311	*Proof.* Follow D′ §4(iii), with T = ⌊2^{(1/4−ε′)n}/n⌋. T enters only the analysis.
   312	- **E_a.** By D′ Lemma 8, |E_a| ≤ (T(T+1)/(n−1))·(P/2+1). Dividing by |S_n| ≥ c₀P²/n² gives
   313	  O(n·T²/P) = O(2^{−2ε′n}/n).
   314	- **E_b.** By Theorem 2, n⁴/H⁴ ≤ 2^{−2ε′n}, and n⁶H^{1/3}N^{−1/6} is far smaller.
   315	- **E_c.** D′ bounds it by C·n·(H^{14/3}P^{1/3}/T + H^{10/3}/P^{1/3}).
   316	  - H^{14/3} ≤ (2n)^{14/3}2^{7ε′n/3} and P^{1/3}/T ≤ 2n·2^{(ε′−1/12)n}. So
   317	    H^{14/3}P^{1/3}/T ≤ (2n)^{6}·2^{(10ε′/3 − 1/12)n}.
   318	  - We need 10ε′/3 − 1/12 < −2ε′, i.e. 16ε′/3 < 1/12, i.e. ε′ < 1/64. For ε′ ≤ 1/80 the
   319	    margin is 1/12 − 16/240 = 1/60. So this term is O(2^{−2ε′n − n/60}·n^{O(1)}).
   320	  - The second term is O(2^{(5ε′/3−1/6)n}).
   321	- **Scale separations.** D′ needs Y > H² and Y⁴ > √2P. Theorem 1 needs Y ≥ 16H² and
