   421	### 4.4 Primes versus integers
   422	
   423	- **Experimentally they agree** (P4 ratio 1.00004).
   424	- **Theorem 1 loses n²** by bounding prime pairs by all integer points. A Selberg presieve
   425	  inside the fourth moment should give C/λ² for S_n (not done; **conjectured**). It changes
   426	  only polylog factors and none of the exponents above.
   427	- **Qualitatively, primality must matter for any e^{−cλ} proof.**
   428	  - The dilates x = t(H, H+1) with gcd(t, ∏𝒫) = 1 are uncovered integer points. Indeed
   429	    F_v(x) = t(BH − A(H+1)) with 0 < |BH − A(H+1)| ≤ H² < Y.
   430	  - There are ≫ P/H of them in the balanced region.
   431	  - So an integer analogue of e^{−cλ} is false once λ ≫ log P (noted by sieve2d_1; checked).
   432	  - Prime pairs are never such dilates.
